{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" = ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix","text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V13MemberIndicesV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","text":"MemberIndices","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V24IncidentHyperedgeIndicesa","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices"}],"roleHeading":"Type Alias","remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L203"},"extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.IncidentHyperedgeIndices","symbolKind":"typealias","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stored row of either plane, read in place."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/IncidentHyperedgeIndices","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/incidenthyperedgeindices"]}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix":{"role":"symbol","title":"IncidenceMatrix","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph: an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a member of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":". The vertices are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" and the columns,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hyperedges, are at positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms run on it unchanged; it is not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" even when built from one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because a cell edit can give a column any number of bits."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/MemberIndices":{"role":"symbol","title":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The indices of the set bits of one stored row, ascending, read in place: a column’s member"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices, or a vertex’s column indices ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices"},{"type":"text","text":"). No copy and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocation, unlike a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"type":"text","text":". It shares the matrix’s words copy-on-write, so a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutation of the matrix leaves it unchanged."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/memberindices"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/IncidentHyperedgeIndices":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/incidenthyperedgeindices","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/IncidentHyperedgeIndices","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.IncidentHyperedgeIndices","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The stored row of either plane, read in place.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"IncidenceMatrixModule","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"}}}